occupations.quals_and_experience:
The applicant must: Have undertaken a mandatory skills assessment if specified in the Migration Legislation. Skills assessments will be conducted by the relevant Skills Assessing Authority;
AND Meet the skill level as defined in ANZSCO;
AND Have at least one (1) year of work experience if applying for a TSS or SESR visa or 3 years of work experience if applying for an ENS visa Work experience must be: in the nominated occupation, or a related occupation at the same skill level. must be undertaken in the last 5 years. full-time or part-time pro-rata. can be while studying through a formal arrangement such as internships, industry and clinical placements, apprenticeships and traineeships, and work experience required through the Job Ready Program. can be served concurrently with any work experience used to substitute for formal qualifications as per ANZSCO requirements, provided that work experience was at the same skill level. In cases where work experience is used to substitute for formal qualifications: Skill Level 2 and 3 occupations, which require 3 years of experience to substitute for a formal qualification, work experience must be undertaken within the last 5 years.

